AUDIO: 'All right, guys. So, this will likely be the quickest video that I\'ve ever made on the channel. It\'s not going to be one of those long videos because the product that we\'re going to talk about today, which is the Truth Ear X, there\'s not a lot to it. Now, it does a lot. It solves'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a lot of different problems when it comes to audio, but it only comes in at $30. It is a little portable DAC amp that has a USB-C connection for you to plug into your phone or your laptop or'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'whatever, and it gives you a 3 1/2 mm plug-in. And the 3 1/2 mm plug-in also supports mic, so if you\'re using a gaming headset or an IEM that has a microphone on the cable, it will pick'

[00:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that up. So, you\'re able to use it for taking phone calls, but the whole idea of this. Now, it\'s convenient as, you know, true wireless earbuds and wireless headphones are, that\'s going to be a lot of people\'s go-to. There\'s so many'

[00:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'people that still feel, and I\'m in this category as well, that you\'re still not getting the same audio quality that you get when you use a wired device. So, the Key X kind of solves that issue because it\'s very, very portable. It even comes'

[01:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'with this little little clip that you I I took this off of here. I don\'t like having it on here, but it gives you this little clip, so you can clip it on a bag or maybe even keep it on your keychain, so you have the Key X with you at all times. And'

[01:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'then outside of that, there\'s nothing in the box. That\'s That is it. But the Key X has a Cirrus Logic CS43131 chip in here. That is actually pretty powerful. I mean, I was able even with'

[01:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'my Beyerdynamic, which is an 80-ohm version, I was able to get plenty of power, plenty of volume just by simply using this. And another little trick that the Key X has up its sleeve that I don\'t see with a lot of other little'

[01:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'portable DACs and amps, is you can simply go into a Chrome browser or Safari or Edge or whatever, and it even has an online EQ tool. And the chip that\'s on the KeyX will just remember'

[01:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'whatever settings that you do within the EQ settings, and it will just apply to whatever you\'re using. Now, I didn\'t use this much because I found that the EQ settings that are on the KeyX just out of the box were already exactly what I'

[02:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'wanted. Plus, different headphones and different IEMs, I would want to go in and, you know, switch around the EQ for every device that I\'m using, and I wanted this to be like just a simple'

